                <invention-title lang="de">HANDSCHALTER UND VERBINDER FÜR EIN ANGETRIEBENES CHIRURGISCHES HANDSTÜCK</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">COMMUTATEUR À MAIN ET CONNECTEUR POUR PIÈCE À MAIN CHIRURGICALE ÉLECTRIQUE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">HANDSWITCH AND CONNECTOR FOR POWERED SURGICAL HANDPIECE</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A surgical tool comprises a power surgical handpiece comprising a longitudinally extending handpiece housing extending along a housing axis and a magnetic field sensor disposed in the housing. The tool further comprises a handswitch comprising a mounting base defining a pivot axis having a direction substantially normal to the housing axis and a mounting surface extending in a first direction, and an elongated lever defining a lever axis substantially normal to the direction of the pivot axis. The lever includes a proximal end pivotably connected to the mounting base at the pivot axis, a distal end opposite the proximal end, a first track on an inner side substantially facing the housing axis, and a second track on an outer side opposite the inner side with both tracks substantially parallel to the lever axis. A spring between the base and the lever biases the lever about the pivot axis. A run-safe switch is slidably disposed on the first track and has a magnet fixed thereto. A lever extension is slidably disposed on the second track.</p>
            </abstract>
